// §14 entry 16 -- same source, different directory/time/locale/hostname ->
// byte-identical output. SHAPE is byte-identical-output, not
// reject-with-a-code: there is no EXS-Exxxx here at all, only a property
// of two builds' bytes.
//
// §9.3: "Byte-identical output for identical inputs across directories,
// times, locales, hostnames." `exsc proba-reproducibilitatem` builds twice
// under deliberately divergent ambient conditions and diffs (ships in v1,
// runs in CI). `tools/reproduce.sh` already implements exactly this
// mechanism -- varying cwd, TZ, LC_ALL/LANG, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, umask and
// (best-effort) hostname -- and this suite's run_conformance_tests reuses
// it rather than reimplementing byte-diffing (this agent's own brief is
// explicit: "tools/reproduce.sh already knows how to do that -- reuse it,
// do not reimplement").
//
// The SOURCE under test does not need anything special -- reproducibility
// is a property of the COMPILER's build process, not of any particular
// program -- so this is deliberately an ordinary, already-valid file
// (`saluta`'s own shape: pure, no `poscit`, per examples/saluta.exsc).
//
// RUNS, as of 2026-09-27. The blocker was never the backend that
// `needs=backend` named: it was that `tools/reproduce.sh` did not compile
// THIS file. It diffed units chosen inside that script, which is evidence
// about those units and not about this entry's source, so a pass here would
// have been the harness reporting on itself.
//
// This fixture is now the script's FOURTH unit: it plus
// examples/imprime.exsc and examples/initium.exsc, emitted with
// `--emitte c --hospes x86_64-linux` in both of the script's divergent
// condition sets and `cmp`ed. `saluta() -> textus` below is the signature
// examples/saluta.exsc declares and `initium` calls, so the substitution
// makes a complete unit that differs from the `saluta` unit in exactly one
// file. Measured on the working tree before this directive was flipped:
// 21,539 bytes, byte-identical across divergent cwd, TZ, LC_ALL/LANG,
// SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, umask and hostname.
//
// STILL OPEN, and not what this entry is graded on: `exsc
// proba-reproducibilitatem` is a stub (exit 4). §9.3 says that subcommand
// ships in v1 and runs in CI; what runs today is the script the subcommand
// is specified to become, called from `run_conformance_tests`'s `bytes`
// shape. The day the subcommand exists, this entry should be re-pointed at
// it and the two compared.

publica functio saluta() -> textus {
    redde "Ave, mundus.";
}

// TEST: entry=16 shape=bytes status=run
